From 2b818000b8b64239e947be1280992bcf8c6e8578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wranked1 <129415993+Wranked1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:01:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix editor deleting other tune_zone settings when changing
 zone number

In the server settings editor, selecting the setting
"tune_zone 2 player_collision 0" and updating it to
"tune_zone 1 player_collision 0" silently deleted an unrelated
"tune_zone 1 gravity 0" setting.

For command settings, CheckCollision only reports a collision (REPLACE)
when an argument with a UNIQUE constraint matches, but when the result
was ADD it still returned the index of the last line that matched a
non-unique argument (here the zone number). The Update button treats
any index other than -1 as a colliding line and, unless it is the
selected line, deletes it. This dates back to the introduction of the
collision check in commit 9cc8a28305e6.

Return -1 when there is no collision, as the function's comment already
documents, so the selected setting is edited in place. Other callers
only act on the index for REPLACE results.

Closes #10852.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E3rsC3FRVop9j9KaM9zRGS
---
 src/game/editor/editor_server_settings.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game/editor/editor_server_settings.cpp b/src/game/editor/editor_server_settings.cpp
index 1b70831b3..c863fe0a6 100644
--- a/src/game/editor/editor_server_settings.cpp
+++ b/src/game/editor/editor_server_settings.cpp
@@ -2026,7 +2026,7 @@ int CMapSettingsBackend::CContext::CheckCollision(const char *pInputString, cons
 
 		// The result is either REPLACE when we found a collision, or ADD
 		Result = Error ? ECollisionCheckResult::REPLACE : ECollisionCheckResult::ADD;
-		return CollidingLineIndex;
+		return Error ? CollidingLineIndex : -1;
 	}
 
 	return -1;
